      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1735 the Dillingersville Union School and Church, a historic landmark, was first built in the village.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zionsville%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Perkiomen Railroad, built in 1876 a mile southeast of Old Zionsville, sparked the founding of Zionsville Station.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        8,
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zionsville%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The West Branch Hosensack Creek bounds Zionsville’s southeast edge, draining into the Perkiomen Creek.",
